==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|elska|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|aliskanan||to care for, cultivate, cherish|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|aliskaz||dear, precious|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{recons|al-||to spur, drive, be enthusiastic|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{recons|el-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|lā-||to drive, move, go|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|elskaði|elskaðu|elskað}}

# to [[love]]
#* ''[[eg elski teg|Eg '''elski''' teg]].''
#*: I love you.
#* ''[[antin|Antin]] '''elskar''' [[tú]] [[tað]], [[ella]] [[hata]]r tú tað.''
#*: Either you love it or you hate it.

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-30|elsk}}

====Antonyms====
* [[hata]]

====Synonyms====
* [[unna]], [[ynna]], [[alska]]

